    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92293.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "All right, well, thank you, Eric, and good afternoon, everyone. As Eric mentioned, this is the seventh and the last installment of our virtual legislative briefing series, at least for the Missouri General Assembly session. It has been quite a ride and appreciate your participation both as members, as well as friends in the Ag community, as well as our friends in the Ag media. We have appreciated your participation and engagement over these sessions. We've covered quite a bit of ground and hopefully you found this information to be useful. Today, we are very, very fortunate to have a true friend of agriculture agriculture and rural Missouri with us with Senator Blount. He's here to give us an update on all things happening in Washington DC. So it looks like he's entering the queue here shortly so we'll be able to have him on shortly. I've also asked B.J. Tanksley today to give us the lowdown on where things are at at this point as we near the end of legislative session. For those of you that are actually watching the video, you can see that he looks as fresh as the beginning of session. His energy level is high and B.J. is sprinting to the finish line on behalf of Farm Bureau to deliver some great wins for us this session. We'll hear a little bit from him as well before we wrap up today. Spencer is also going to be on to give us an update on federal issues and we'll recap a discussion on broadband that we had yesterday with a subcommittee of the House Transportation and Infrastructure Committee. That's what's on tap for the session today. At this point, let's see, Senator Blodking, you hear us? I can't.",
