    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92293.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Well, it would be easy to have a bipartisan infrastructure bill on a couple of the Sunday morning shows a month ago. This is a point I made. If this was about infrastructure, you could almost guarantee a bipartisan victory on infrastructure. And why wouldn't the administration want that? But only about 20% or so of the so-called infrastructure bill deals with roads, bridges, highways, airports, ports. broadband and even the underground infrastructure, water lines and things like that. I think Republicans would be glad to join the president on all of those issues. And most of those, by the way, have a way that they either totally or largely pay for themselves. You build that on top of the highway trust fund that we collect. If you're going to do something in a rural or urban water district, do it in a way that you give people plenty of time to pay that improvement back over their utility bill. So maybe all it cost you is writing down the the interest to where the government subsidizes the interest, but the people that use the water companies still pay for that. There's a lot of public private potential out there. That kind of infrastructure bill we really need. We need it in the waterways in our state. We understand that the inland ports are critically important in Missouri these days, the Missouri General Assembly with the active incurries where the Farm Bureau has stepped up in the last five years or so in ways they have it before on that issue. And an infrastructure bill, it's about infrastructure would be one thing. Now, when you ask people, are you for an infrastructure bill, I think they know we need that. They know the government needs to do it. And so they say, well, yes, we're for it. And then the next thing you hear is some reporter expressing that, well, You know, 40% of all Republicans or maybe 60% of all Republicans say they're for the President's infrastructure bill without knowing that the infrastructure bill also includes a whole lot of things that maybe we should do and maybe we should debate, but we shouldn't do them under the guise that somehow they're infrastructure.",
