    "turn_text": "Well, again, I think you need to be sure that the people that work for you in Washington, understand the real impact this has. What does it mean to a farm that's decided to, or a business that's decided to change their corporate structure because the suddenly the rate was appealing and the various deductions were appealing and even more appealing in some cases for small business, the ability to write off a certain amount for depreciation, the issues that relate to inventory and other things really important in the tax bill that passed in 2017. you know, not think that somehow Two more years of higher education or two more years of education before kindergarten are going to come for free. Are they going to be part of the local school district? If they are, you're going to have to build more building space. Is the federal government going to come in and do that for you when the federal government comes in? Are they going to bring all kinds of rules and regulations to your school system that you would prefer not be there and that the local school board would have never adopted? I think we're looking at a case here where from virtually the time you're born until you leave the world, the current administration appears to think that there's an important role for government in every step of that process.",
