      {
        "text": "Democrats do not want to repeat their past mistake of missing opportunities during the first two years of Obama's presidency.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "Joe Manchin, both Democratic senators from Arizona, and John Tester oppose changing the legislative process to allow a bare majority to alter laws and regulations.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      },
      {
        "text": "These key Democrats believe maintaining minority protections is essential due to anticipated Republican gains.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      },
      {
        "text": "A bare majority could enact changes that would harm constituents represented by these Democrats.",
