        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Connecting national policies to rural livelihoods like farming strengthens legitimacy and trust in governance.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Public recognition of service enhances civic cohesion and reinforces positive political culture.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Expressing gratitude publicly serves a rhetorical purpose in building rapport or influence.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Agree / Align"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92293,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92293.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, great to be with all of you. I appreciate our friendship both personally and with the Farm Bureau, our whole team, Derek Coats, And my team in the state, as well as our team here, Andrew Lassidy, our tax folks who are looking at these tax issues that can affect you so carefully. And so significantly, I want to continue to have all of the input we can have so that we have examples of the kind of real world impact of these decisions that people act like they're making in an ivory tower. So thanks for letting me be with you today. I've got another vote to go to right now, which is a vote on a water bill that we're going to pass with a significant bipartisan majority. We could do the same thing with other infrastructure project bills if President Biden would allow us to put the true infrastructure package together and see some dirt moving here pretty quickly as we begin to do the work we need to do to take advantage of the location we have and location the country has. So thanks for letting me be with you.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
